From: Arthur Clark <mydevstuff@mail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 20:29:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/33] QNX: enable Draw/Impress via system NSS

Draw and Impress (the sd module) hard-link xmlsecurity, which needs a
crypto backend. The bundled NSS is unbuilt and unported on QNX, so point
xmlsecurity at the apk-provided system nss/nspr with --with-system-nss.

This sets SYSTEM_NSS=TRUE and drops bundled NSS from BUILD_TYPE; ENABLE_NSS
stays TRUE. The change is config-only and invalidates no already-built
module (Writer/Calc/Math/vcl/svx/sfx unchanged). It matches the Alpine
--with-tls=nss posture, so system nss/nspr become build+runtime deps.

Change-Id: I8fe859d7f54e50242ef3751cf65e4a3bb2fe2f58
---
 distro-configs/LibreOfficeQNX.conf | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/distro-configs/LibreOfficeQNX.conf b/distro-configs/LibreOfficeQNX.conf
index 6408fbfe9..2e07d5e9d 100644
--- a/distro-configs/LibreOfficeQNX.conf
+++ b/distro-configs/LibreOfficeQNX.conf
@@ -31,3 +31,4 @@
 --with-system-lcms2
 --with-system-boost
 --with-system-openssl
+--with-system-nss
